}}|subdivision_type1=[[Communities of Balisca|Community]]|subdivision_name1={{flag|Cerdanya}}|area_km2=1,477,700|population_census=127,686|population_census_year=2025|regional_languages=|common_languages={{W|Catalan language|Volisanian}}, [[w:Occitan language|Beron]]<br />{{small|Minorities: [[w:Mapuche language|Walldungu]] and {{W|Yaghan language|Yámanakuta}}}}|cctld=.cdp|government_type={{W|Liquid democracy}} with {{W|Legislature|regional council}}|mapsize=280px|subdivision_type2=|subdivision_name2=|ethnic_groups_year=2023|ethnic_groups=42.7% [[Baliscans]]<br/> 57.3% [[Demographics of Balisca|others]]|population_census_rank=44th}}'''Cap de Pingüins''' ({{Literal translation|Cape of Penguins}}), is one of the [[Regions of Balisca|ten regions]] of the [[Cerdanya|Cerdanyan]] [[Communities of Balisca|community]] within the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It is the least populous, largest by area, northernmost and westernmost region of Balisca. The region's capital and largest city is [[Punta Jaumandreu]].

The territory of Cap dels Pingüins includes Balisca's claimed [[Baliscan Arktici]] (this claim is suspended as part of the [[Arktici Treaty]]). The [[Aurora Islands]] (''Könāgū'' in [[W:Yaghan language|Yámanakuta]]), and the [[Boreal Islands]] are administered by Cap de Pingüins, and form the [[Illes de Tinguiririca]] ("Isles of Tinguiririca") [[Cantons of Balisca|canton]]. The regional administration is seated in Punta Jaumandreu and the assembly designates a delegate for the Arktici sector. The "civil power" of any of the administrators extends no further than Balisca's own bases.

The territory of the current region had been visited by indigenous people (most notably the {{W|Yaghan people|Yaghans}}) for more than 12,000 years, since they migrated to the south of Tinguiririca. It was first encountered by Illypnian explorers in 1520 when spotted by the expedition of Volisanian explorer [[Tomàs Jaumandreu]]. Due to the region's significance to unrestricted navigation through the [[x Passage]], it was contested between the [[Volisan Empire|Volisan]], [[Breislandic Empire|Breislandic]] and [[Aetolian Empire|Aetolian]] empires during the 18th century, which was a significant factor in the recognition of the [[Commonwealth of Cerdanya]]. 

